<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Madison is seen on the morning of discharge after 72 hours of video-EEG monitoring. Two of his usual events were recorded, the second on the third evening after a night of sleep deprivation, and he confirmed on review of the video that both were typical. His MRI last week was normal. Dr. Okafor-Haverford of neurology reviewed the recordings with him yesterday and explained the diagnosis, and the neuropsychiatric assessment on the unit found generalized anxiety and a moderate depressive episode. He says he is relieved that it is not epilepsy, though he wonders how something that feels so real could come from the mind; he asked good questions and has read the written explanation. He has had no thoughts of death or self-harm, and the rifle has been locked away with the ammunition stored separately since his first visit. He has not driven since then. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Video-EEG</td><td>Two habitual events captured; normal EEG throughout both</td></tr><tr><td>MRI</td><td>Normal</td></tr><tr><td>Mood and anxiety</td><td>PHQ-9 12; GAD-7 13</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts; rifle locked; not driving</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Tired after a night of sleep deprivation; no fever</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No palpitations, chest pain, or exertional faintness</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>Two recorded events; no headache, weakness, or numbness</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Low mood, worry, and irritability on levetiracetam; no suicidal thoughts, elevated mood, or psychotic symptoms</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

